WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:03.960
You probably know your blood type -- A?

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.080
B?

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.640
Universal donor?

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.460
You might even carry a card on you

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.220
so that in case of emergency,

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.120
you won’t get the wrong type of blood.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.740
But do you know how your blood type

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.460
was actually identified in the first place?

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.600
Blood type can be determined in two ways:

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.260
forward blood grouping which detects markers

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.260
on the blood cells themselves,

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.740
And reverse blood grouping,

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.580
which detects antibodies present

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.820
in the blood plasma

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.180
Either type of test today takes a long time,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.980
requires technical training, and can be expensive

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.080
Researchers have been working

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.600
on a new blood typing test

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.100
that is not only easy to use,

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.740
but can be done on site --

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.940
in as little as 30 seconds

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.320
A small blood sample is dropped

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.640
into the middle of the testing strip

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.500
A color change in either observation window

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.500
delivers the results

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.760
This test can perform forward

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:53.760
and reverse blood grouping

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.300
at the same time which gives

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.620
more confidence in the result

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.140
A similar test can also be used

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.160
to determine rare blood types

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.200
After the blood is loaded onto the disc,  the blood

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.500
spectroscopy is used to automatically

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.160
determine the blood type,

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.180
So a person doesn’t need

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:09.740
to interpret the color change

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:10.920
and the test can be done by someone

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.080
who is colorblind

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.020
Until now paper-based tests were reliant

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:16.120
on blood samples that had already been spun in

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:19.800
a centrifuge, which takes time and experience.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.560
The introduction of these test strips

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:22.640
has the potential to not only

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.600
save time and money in the hospital

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.800
but in remote areas with few resources,

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:29.000
rapid blood typing could be done by non-trained

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.420
users and blood supplies can be stretched

